# ai.wing — Change Log

Append-only record of AI-made changes so any entry can be reverted precisely.
This project is **not** under git, so this file is the only revert history.

Format per entry:

    ## [NNN] YYYY-MM-DD — Short title
    Scope:   files touched
    Change:  what changed, specifically
    Revert:  exact steps to undo

---

## [001] 2026-07-27 — Hero: scroll-scrubbed assembly + premium animation layer

**Scope**
- `components/Hero.tsx`
- `app/globals.css`

**Change**

1. **Scroll-scrubbed assembly timeline** (`Hero.tsx`, in `useGSAP`, added after the
   trust-icon idle-float block). A `scrub: 1` timeline bound to the hero's own
   scroll span. Reversible on scroll-up. Layers separate in depth as the hero
   exits:
   - headline line 1 → `yPercent -14, z 60`
   - headline line 2 (accent) → `yPercent -26, z 120` (trails line 1)
   - sub-copy → `yPercent -18`
   - offer chip → `yPercent -26, rotate -1.5`
   - form → `yPercent -10` (holds longest; it's the conversion target)
   - trust rail → `yPercent -34`, staggered 0.04 so it unthreads L→R

   All tweens drive **transform only** — never opacity alone — so a throttled
   ticker or an un-fired trigger can't strand copy invisible.

2. **Typographic accent animation** (same block). Per-character weight shimmer on
   the accent line: each char scales to 1.06 and lifts 4% in sequence
   (`stagger.each 0.045`, yoyo, `repeatDelay 3.4`). Transform-driven.

3. **Headline line tags** (`Hero.tsx` JSX, ~line 334/339). Added
   `data-hero-line="1"` and `data-hero-line="2"` to the two `SplitLine` wrapper
   spans so the assembly timeline can address them independently.

4. **Sub-headline humanised** (`Hero.tsx`, `[data-hero-sub]`). Official claims
   preserved verbatim (100 Mbps*, unlimited data**); phrasing warmed:
   added "reaching homes the cable companies never will" and "right where you
   live".

5. **Brand token `--color-brand-space: #05103A`** (`globals.css` `@theme`).
   Sampled from hughesnet.com's live computed styles.

6. **`.surface-a` graded** (`globals.css`). Was a flat
   `background-color: var(--color-brand-blue-dark)`. Now additionally carries
   `background-image: linear-gradient(180deg, brand-blue-dark 0%, #0A2C55 55%,
   brand-space 100%)` so the hero sky gains depth toward the foot.

**Source of truth for colors/content**
Scraped live from <https://www.hughesnet.com/> this session:
- `#DE3700` CTA orange · `#0096FA` h1/link blue · `#005DAC` logo blue
- `#154A8E` / `#0E4275` navies · `#53565A` body ink · `#05103A` deep space (new)
- H1: "Hughesnet Satellite Internet for Rural America"
- Hero claims: "Unlimited, high-speed satellite internet!", "FREE Professional
  Installation†", "Price Guarantee", "24/7 Live Customer Care", "Affordable
  Plans", "SAVE $25/mo. for 12 months!^", "up to 100 Mbps*", phone 855-543-5405

**Revert**
1. `Hero.tsx` — delete the `SCROLL-SCRUBBED ASSEMBLY` block (the `assembly`
   timeline) and the `Typographic accent` block (the `accentChars` tween).
2. `Hero.tsx` — remove `data-hero-line="1"` / `data-hero-line="2"` attributes
   from the two headline wrapper spans.
3. `Hero.tsx` — restore sub-headline to:
   `Unlimited, high-speed satellite internet — with fast speeds up to 100 Mbps*
   and unlimited data**, available where you live.`
4. `globals.css` — remove the `--color-brand-space` token and its comment.
5. `globals.css` — restore `.surface-a` to `background-color` only (delete the
   `background-image` gradient and the added comment lines).

