--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[011] — Hero video sizing: contain plate, badges pinned to the footage
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

**Scope** — `components/hero/OrbitScene.tsx` only. CSS/layout, no re-encode.

**Problem** — `object-cover` scales the footage UP to fill the section. The hero
is not 16:9, so the video was magnified ~11% on tall viewports and ~13% on wide
short ones, which enlarged the satellite and pushed the house/horizon off the
bottom of the fold. Worst at short laptop heights, exactly as reported.

**Fix** — the video now lives in a 16:9 "plate" sized to *fit*, and a second
plate of identical geometry carries the HUD, so badge percentages are
percentages **of the footage** and stay pinned to satellite/beam/house at any
viewport instead of drifting with the letterboxing.

Sizing took three attempts; the first two silently broke the 16:9 box:
1. `aspect-video h-full w-auto max-h/max-w` — `h-full` is an *explicit* height
   and overrides `aspect-ratio`. At 1920×1080 the plate measured 1180×920
   (ratio **1.28**), so `object-cover` inside it was cropping again.
2. `aspect-video w-full max-h/max-w` — `max-height` clamps the height but does
   **not** pull the width in. At 1440×780 the plate measured 1180×620
   (ratio **1.90**). Still cropping.
3. **Shipped:** every constraint folded into a single `min()` on *width*, with
   `aspect-ratio` deriving the height —
   `w-[min(94%,1180px,calc((100svh-10rem)*16/9))]`. Width is the sole driver, so
   the ratio survives all three constraints.
   · `1180px` holds the satellite near 295px rather than growing with the viewport.
   · `(100svh-10rem)*16/9` is the height budget expressed as a width. The 10rem
     looks generous because the hero itself runs past the fold at 660px tall and
     the plate centres in the section, so the budget must absorb that offset,
     not just the navbar.

Badge coordinates retuned to plate-relative: Mbps `left 70% / top 38%`,
Unlimited `left 72% / top 62%`, Signal Locked `left 57% / top 73%` — the last
placed right of the beam, which crosses x≈52% at that height.

Deliberately **not** `transform: scale()`: it would shrink the HUD layer's type
along with the footage. Capping the box shrinks only the video; the badges keep
their own font sizes (verified 16/24/16px unchanged across all three viewports).

**Verified — measured at three viewports**
| viewport | plate | ratio | satellite | horizon vs fold |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1920×1080 | 1180×664 | 1.777 | 295px | 767 / 1080 |
| 1440×780  | 1102×620 | 1.777 | 276px | 677 / 780  |
| 1366×660  | 889×500  | 1.778 | 222px | 638 / 660 (22px clear) |

All three: `is16by9` true · house and horizon inside the fold · all three badges
inside the fold · all three clear of the beam (checked by solving the beam's x at
each badge's mid-height) · badge font sizes unchanged.

Contrast re-measured at 1366×660 after the geometry change, sampling real video
pixels through the scrim: headline **17.89**, Mbps **14.32**, Unlimited **12.90**,
Signal Locked **17.53**. AA needs 4.5, AAA 7.

**Not verified** — playback. The pane reports `document.hidden: true` and
browsers will not advance media in a hidden document, so framing is confirmed
from the poster frame but the loop running still needs a real browser.

**Revert** — restore `PLATE` in `components/hero/OrbitScene.tsx` to
`'absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover object-[68%_center]'` on the video
with the HUD positioned against the section rather than a plate.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[012] — Hero: true full-bleed video, anchored HUD, headline movement removed
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

**Scope** — `components/hero/OrbitScene.tsx`, `components/Hero.tsx`.

**A · Full-bleed video (reverses [011]'s contain plate)**
[011] fitted the video into a letterboxed 16:9 plate, which is what produced the
visible edge on the right. The video is now `absolute left-0 top-0 w-full h-full
object-cover object-center`, filling the section corner to corner.

Because `object-fit: cover` crops a *different slice of the frame at every
viewport*, the badges can no longer be static CSS percentages — under [011] they
were percentages of a plate that matched the footage exactly; under cover that
assumption is gone. They are now resolved through the same transform the browser
applies to the video (`k = max(w/1280, h/720)`, centred overflow), recomputed on
mount, on `ResizeObserver`, and on `resize`. Anchors are held in source-frame
coordinates (`BADGE_ANCHORS`), each picked to clear the beam at its own height.
Positions are written as `left`/`top`, **not** transform — GSAP owns the badges'
transform for the entrance stagger and would fight it.

Badges are clamped to the *visible band* (`min(hostHeight, innerHeight - hostTop)`),
not the host's full height. Without that the Signal Locked pill anchored
correctly to the house but landed at y659/bottom 685 on a 660px viewport — off
screen. Clamped it sits at y613/bottom 644.

**B · Video asset — nothing to swap**
The attached file is **byte-identical** to the one already in the project:
2,618,227 bytes, mtime 17:59, `md5 ea00b373f3fddbb0485627b309bca9ba`, same
1280×720 / 10.005s. The de-watermarked version did not come through, so
`public/media/hero-orbit.mp4` is unchanged (still the [010] crossfaded re-cut,
9.125s, 36 dB seam).

**C · Headline movement removed**
Two separate sources, not one:
1. The entrance `.from('[data-hero-chars] [data-char]', { yPercent: 120,
   rotateX: -75, opacity: 0 })` — the per-character rise.
2. **An infinite idle tween** on `[data-hero-line="2"]` ("for Rural America"):
   `gsap.to(accentChars, { scale: 1.06, yPercent: -4, repeat: -1, yoyo: true,
   repeatDelay: 3.4 })`. This was the recurring bounce; removing only the
   entrance would have left it running.
Both deleted. The headline is now simply present — no transform, no fade.
An interim version used a per-char `from(opacity: 0)` fade, which measured
`anyOpacityZero: true` in a pane with no rAF frames: 35 characters invisible if
the timeline never runs. Given this project has already had text blanked by
animating its legibility, that was dropped too. The copy block around it still
fades as a whole. Scroll-tied parallax on `[data-hero-line]` is untouched.

**Verified at 1366×660 after a hard reload**
Headline: 35 chars, `allOpaque: true`, `allNoTransform: true`, `minOpacity: 1`,
and no positional change sampled 1200 ms apart (idle bounce confirmed gone).
Video: `fullBleed: true` (video box === section box), `object-fit: cover`,
`object-position: 50% 50%`, `duration 9.125`, `error: null`, loop + muted set.
HUD: all three placed by the hook, all inside the fold, all clear of the beam.
Also checked at 1440×780 and 1920×1080 — full-bleed true at both, all badges
placed, in fold and clear of the beam.
`npx tsc --noEmit` exit 0.

**Regression accepted, and it is a real one:** at 1366×660 the house (y685) and
horizon (y733) now sit **below the fold**. Full-bleed cover fills the section,
and the hero section is 798 px tall on a 660 px viewport because its own content
is that tall — so the lower third of the composition is simply below the fold.
[011]'s contain plate kept them visible; that was the trade being made for the
letterbox edge. Fixing it properly means shortening the hero, not resizing the
video. Flagged rather than silently reverted, since full-bleed was the explicit ask.

**Not verified** — playback. `document.hidden: true` in the pane; browsers will
not advance media in a hidden document.

**Revert** — A: restore the `PLATE`/`PLATE_WRAP` plate from [011] and drop
`useCoverAnchors` + the badge refs. C: restore the two GSAP blocks in
`Hero.tsx` (the `[data-hero-chars] [data-char]` `.from` and the `accentChars`
idle tween).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[013] — New hero video; hero seam + scroll-fade fixes; WhyChoose hover/glow
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

**Scope** — `components/hero/OrbitScene.tsx`, `components/Hero.tsx`,
`components/Navbar.tsx`, `components/WhyChoose.tsx`, `app/globals.css`,
`public/media/hero-orbit.*`.

**Video swapped.** The watermark-free file did arrive this time —
`md5 c5c6ed70…` vs the previous `ea00b373…`, 1.92 MB vs 2.62 MB, same
1280×720 / 10.005s. Ran through the same tail-over-head crossfade as [010];
shipped file is 9.125s, 1.33 MB, loop seam **36.02 dB**.

**Seam at the right edge — it was not the video.** Measured: video width 1356 =
`document.documentElement.clientWidth` = section width, left 0. `w-screen`
computes to the same 1356, because content cannot paint under the scrollbar.
The bright strip was the **custom scrollbar track** (`::-webkit-scrollbar-track:
#F4F6F8` in globals) reading as a light rail against the near-black hero. Track
is now `transparent`; the thumb is untouched. `w-screen` reverted to `w-full`
since it gains nothing and can overflow on browsers that count the scrollbar in
100vw.

**Seam at the header boundary.** The navbar is white 0.8–0.95 with `border-b`
plus a drop shadow; against the dark hero that border was the visible line. Both
border and shadow now animate to fully transparent in the unscrolled state and
back when scrolled. Deliberately did **not** make the navbar transparent: its
links are `#003A70` on white and it is `fixed` over mostly-light sections, so
transparency would need a per-section colour inversion — a much larger change
than the reported symptom.

**Hero scroll fade removed.** `contentOpacity = useTransform(scrollYProgress,
[0,0.65],[1,0])` deleted and dropped from the copy block's style. Parallax y/x
retained. Verified the block's inline style is now exactly `transform:none` —
no opacity channel at all.

**WhyChoose additions**
1. *Text entrance* — the clip wipe now carries a slight lateral slide
   (`x: ±20 → 0`) alongside `clipPath`, still starting on the same frame as its
   icon, still staggered per card. No opacity involved.
2. *Hover* — lift `y: -4` (spring), border brightens, and a radial brand-blue
   glow fades in **behind** the pair. The glow is a `::before` on the pair with
   `z-index: -1` under `isolate`, so it can never wash over the copy.
   **Structural change forced here:** the pair was a single `motion.div` already
   carrying `x/y` pointer drift, and a hover lift also wants `y`. Two animations
   cannot write one element's `y`, so the pair is now three nodes —
   outer `div` (layout + hover target + glow context) › drift `motion.div` ›
   lift `motion.div`.
3. *Background* — `.wc-glowfield` adds two counter-drifting radial fields to the
   section on 26s/34s loops, transform-driven, behind the content.
All three respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.

**Verified** — `npx tsc --noEmit` exit 0 · no error overlay · video full-bleed
(`full: true`), duration 9.125, `error: null` · hero copy inline style
`transform:none` · all headline chars at opacity 1 · 5 pairs, glowfield present,
5 lift wrappers · navbar border and shadow both transparent at rest.

**Not verified** — playback and the hover/idle motion: the pane reports
`document.hidden: true` (media will not advance) and renders no rAF frames.

**Revert** — restore `contentOpacity` in `Hero.tsx`; put the navbar's
`borderColor`/shadow back; restore `::-webkit-scrollbar-track: #F4F6F8`; collapse
the WhyChoose pair back to one `motion.div` and delete the `.wc-glowfield` /
`[data-wc-pair]::before` blocks from globals.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[014] — Four sections rebuilt for structural uniqueness
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

**Scope** — `components/Technology.tsx`, `components/Features.tsx`,
`components/HowItWorks.tsx`, `components/ResellerBenefits.tsx`,
new `components/features/RadialNetwork.tsx`, `app/globals.css`.
**Deleted:** `components/features/DeviceStage.tsx`.

**1 · JUPITER — spec-sheet reveal, vertical sequential gate**
Three per-fact ScrollTriggers replaced by ONE scrubbed timeline with each row in
its own 1-unit slot. A row's underline completes at slot+0.95 and the next row
begins at slot+1, so this is a genuine gate — the previous per-row triggers
could overlap whenever rows were close together. Underline is an SVG line with
`pathLength={1}`, `strokeDasharray="1"`, drawn left-to-right; it replaced the
CSS hover-width bar. Row spacing py-7 → py-11. Body copy reveals with
`clipPath` + `y`, never opacity alone. Photos: each wrapper gained
`overflow-hidden rounded-xl` and `[data-tech-photo]:hover img { scale(1.05) }`
in globals, so the zoom is clipped to the frame and moves the image only; the
existing `photoY` scroll parallax is retained.

**2 · Connected life — radial hub-and-spoke**
`DeviceStage` deleted, replaced by `RadialNetwork.tsx`: router hub at the centre
of a 0 0 400 400 viewBox, four devices on a 128px ring at 0/90/180/270°. Spokes
are trimmed at both ends (`inner 36`, `outer RING-44`) so they spring from the
hub's edge and stop at the device rather than running under either. Sequence per
spoke: line draws (`strokeDashoffset` 1→0, 0.42s), then its device scales in
**at at+0.42** — gated on the line arriving, not run alongside it. After settling,
a second overlaid `[data-rn-flow]` line carries travelling dashes; it must be a
separate element because a repeating dasharray would overwrite the `dasharray="1"`
the draw-in depends on (same trap as the WhyChoose connectors). Three hub rings
pulse outward on a stagger. Structure is radial — distinct from the hero's single
beam and JUPITER's rows. Removed the now-dangling `[data-ds-device]` entrance and
all `[data-ds-*]` ambient tweens; verified 0 orphan references.

**3 · Signal locked — bars promoted, cards demoted**
Analyser height h-14 → h-40/lg:h-52, the percentage figure text-5xl → text-7xl/
lg:text-8xl, dish 16 → 24. Step cards reduced to secondary weight: padding
p-5 → p-3.5, icon tile 11 → 8, gap 4 → 2.5, shadow softened, and the connecting
rail thinned from 2px to 1px. Bars now grow from `scaleY: 0` in sequence, and the
card row is gated behind them with `'>-0.05'` — the readout completes first.
Removed the old bar flicker tween: it wrote on the same elements as the grow-in
and would have fought it.

**4 · Local Advantage — directional panel slide**
Tab/underline structure untouched, as specified. Added `AnimatePresence` with
`mode="popLayout"` (so the outgoing panel cannot push the incoming one down while
both are mounted) and a `prevActive` ref deriving direction: a tab to the right
enters from +20px and exits to -20px, reversed for leftward moves. 0.34s.

**Verified after all four** — `npx tsc --noEmit` exit 0 · no Next error overlay ·
9 sections render · JUPITER 3 facts / 3 underlines / 3 photos · radial svg with
1 hub, 4 lines, 4 flows, 4 nodes, 0 stale `[data-ds-*]` · signal 1 meter /
40 bars / 4 cards · Local Advantage panel mounts ("Official Partnership",
"Commitment 01 / 05") · **0 stranded elements** (no `visibility: hidden`, no
zero-matrix) across all rebuilt sections · no horizontal overflow.

**Not verified** — the motion itself. The pane renders no rAF frames, so scrubbed
timelines and idle loops do not advance there; structure, build and DOM are
confirmed, pacing needs a real browser.

**Revert** — per section, independently: 1 restore the per-fact
`forEach` timeline + hover-width underline span in `Technology.tsx`; 2 restore
`DeviceStage.tsx` and its import/ambient tweens in `Features.tsx`, delete
