[015] — Hero header/hero seam fixed properly; sections 2 & 3 of [014] reverted
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

**Scope** — `app/page.tsx`, `components/Hero.tsx`, `components/Navbar.tsx`,
`app/globals.css`, `components/HowItWorks.tsx`.

**The seam — actual root cause, missed in [013].**
[013] treated the symptoms (nav border, scrollbar track) but not the cause:
`app/page.tsx` had `<main className="flex-1 mt-20">`, reserving 80px above the
hero. The hero therefore *started below* the fixed white navbar, so the boundary
was a white bar butted against a dark hero — no amount of border removal fixes
that. Now: `mt-20` dropped from `main`, hero padding `pt-8/lg:pt-10` →
`pt-28/lg:pt-32` so its copy still clears the bar, and the video runs from y=0
behind the header. Measured `heroTop: 0`, `videoTop: 0`,
`videoCoversHeader: true`.

**Navbar blended over the hero,** which [013] declined to do and should have.
`data-atop={!isScrolled}` on the nav; unscrolled it animates to
`rgba(255,255,255,0)` with `blur(0px)` and its ink inverts to white via
`nav[data-atop='true'] .nav-ink`. Scrolled onto the light sections it returns to
the white bar with `#003A70` ink. The inversion is the part that makes
transparency safe — navy links on the footage would be unreadable.
Verified by disabling transitions: at top ink is `rgb(255,255,255)`, past the
hero it is `rgb(0,58,112)`. White nav ink measures **17.69** contrast against the
video beneath it.

**Hero scroll fade** — already removed in [013]; re-confirmed the copy block's
inline style is exactly `transform:none` and `h1` opacity is 1.

**WhyChoose** — already added in [013]; re-confirmed live: `.wc-glowfield`
present, hover `::before` is a radial gradient at `z-index: -1` (behind copy,
never over it), 5 lift wrappers, clip-path text reveal in place.

